<title>GERMANY: E-Plus has 500,000 subscribers.</title>
<headline>E-Plus has 500,000 subscribers.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German mobile telephone operator E-Plus Mobilfunk GmbH said it had 500,000 subscribers at the end of 1996, up from 200,000 a year earlier.</p>
<p>E-Plus, owned by Veba AG, Thyssen AG, BellSouth and Vodafone, said the strong growth was due to the rapid expansion of its nationwide network, which now reaches 90 percent of the German population.  </p>
<p>E-Plus said it had invested about three billion marks in its network to date, a figure that would rise to four billion marks by the end of this year.</p>
<p>The company will create 300 new jobs, raising its workforce to 2,500.</p>
<p>The company also said the market had responded positively to the advantageous pricing structure it introduced in November.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
